Let livecd-tools/appliance-creator build for a foreign architecture.

With LIVECD_FORCEARCH=armv6hl in the environment, dnf resolves and installs
armv6hl packages into the install root from an x86_64/aarch64 host, exactly
like 'mock --forcearch'. The rpm scriptlets and the kickstart %post are then
executed inside the install root through binfmt_misc (qemu-user-static
registered with the 'F' flag). dnf and rpm themselves keep running natively.

Generated against livecd-tools 31.0 (python3-imgcreate-31.0-15.el9).

--- a/imgcreate/dnfinst.py
+++ b/imgcreate/dnfinst.py
@@ -100,6 +100,15 @@ class DnfLiveCD(dnf.Base):
         self.conf.prepend_installroot("cachedir")
         self.conf.prepend_installroot("persistdir")
         self.conf.install_weak_deps = not excludeWeakdeps
+        # Cross-architecture builds (like 'mock --forcearch'): resolve and
+        # install packages for the architecture in LIVECD_FORCEARCH. The rpm
+        # scriptlets and the kickstart %post then run in the install root
+        # through binfmt_misc (qemu-user-static registered with the 'F' flag).
+        forcearch = os.environ.get("LIVECD_FORCEARCH")
+        if forcearch:
+            logging.info("Forcing target architecture %s", forcearch)
+            self.conf.arch = forcearch
+            self.conf.ignorearch = True
         if cacheonly:
